    section3Body: "Enquiries for pagdi tying appointment in Pune generally come from people in one of a few situations: actively finalising wedding vendors with a confirmed date, researching options before anything is locked in, or coordinating on behalf of someone else — a family member, or a professional wedding planner managing a client's full vendor list. We treat all of these the same way at the enquiry stage: share what you know so far, even if it's incomplete, and we'll respond with whatever is useful at that stage, whether that's firm availability and pricing or just general guidance while you're still deciding. Planners working across multiple bookings are welcome to reach out directly without the couple needing to be involved in the initial conversation. If you're helping arrange things for someone else, it's worth including their contact details once a specific package and colour direction needs confirming, since that decision is usually easiest to finalise with the person who'll actually be wearing the safa.",
    section4Title: "What's included and how pricing works",
    section4Body: "What determines the final price for pagdi tying appointment in Pune comes down to guest count, fabric selection, styling complexity and travel distance if the venue is outside our regular service area. A groom-only booking with a simple fold is at the lower end of the range; a full wedding party package with premium fabric and detailed accessory work is at the higher end — most bookings fall somewhere in between depending on the actual event. Every quote includes the artist's time and full coordination of the tying schedule; fabric can be included in the package or, if you already have fabric chosen, we can quote tying-only pricing instead. Kalgi, brooch and similar accessories are usually priced as optional additions. We'd always recommend sharing your real numbers — date, venue, headcount, fabric preference — rather than asking for a starting price in isolation, since that's what lets us give you something you can actually plan a budget around.",
